      "type": "IMPLEMENTATION_FIDELITY_LIMITATION",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "description": "Source code implementations in src/filter_aware.py (ACORN, SIEVE, UNIFY) are paper-inspired approximations evaluated on a single shared HNSW graph, rather than the official vendor C++/CUDA frameworks from SIGMOD/VLDB.",
      "root_cause": "- ACORN (Patel et al. 2024) constructs a specialized gamma-scaled edge graph; our baseline approximates query-time traversal via 2-hop neighbor expansion.\n- SIEVE (Gao et al. 2024) builds a multi-index collection with a 3D packing model; our baseline approximates centroid entry routing by sampling 16 candidates.\n- UNIFY (Liang et al. 2024) constructs a Segmented Inclusive Graph (SIG); our baseline uses a heuristic rule switching between InGraph and ACORN with increased ef.",
      "resolution": "Must be explicitly disclosed in the paper methodology. These methods must be described as 'paper-inspired single-graph heuristic baselines', not as official vendor implementations.",
      "status": "LIMITATION FORMALLY DOCUMENTED"
    }
  ],
